ons for patients  with et  or mf and the jack 2 exon  12 mutations for patients with pv and  the molecular testing  using multi gene and gs panel  including those genes are recommended  there is also guidelines from cab and  ash for aml genetic testing  recommendations  it is also recommended very similar to  the ansing guideline  that include karyotype and fish and also  molecular testing for all or most of the  cases  with those mutations i just mentioned  which is very similar to the ncc  guideline for selected  selected cases the kit for core binding  factor leukemia and also for apl  we have to do the pml rara test  next i'm going to talk about genetic  abnormalities in  aml this is a very busy figure  if you look at on the left side there  are many many  genes their mutations  are commonly seen in aml patients  you can see how the percentage  represents the incidence  in the aml on the right side  side of the slide there are many many  translocations  associated with aml patients  some of the mutation coexisting  with the chance locations that will  change the prognostic  information or the treatment  the treatment associated with myeloid  biomarker testing  let's look at the disease for aml  the biomarkers include fleet 3 idh1  and 2. the s used are pcr and  nds and also the drug on the right  side of the column for cml  and apl there are bcr-801  and pm aurora chains locations  the acids include the pcr phase  karyotype ngs and also there's drugs  on the right side and the apl  used the atra for example for the pv  the jack 2 mutation analysis  is recommended to use pcr or nds method  and use the drug is also listed here  for so many different biomarkers and  tests in  these patients tests usually performed  sequentially and it takes a long time to  give results  it uses many samples instead of one  therefore ngs is the solution to reduce  number of assays turnaround time and the  sample size  if you think about the figure i showed  in the previous slide for